{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/424040-requiem-2nd-ed-vs-cr\u00faac-sorcery-what-is-canon","id":424040,"title":"Requiem 2nd Ed vs Cr\u00faac Sorcery: What Is Canon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-01T06:09:33-08:00","id":424040,"title":"Requiem 2nd Ed vs Cr\u00faac Sorcery: What Is Canon?","content":"I was having a conversation the other day about the differences between the Cr\u00faac Sorcery in the first edition and the second and a few things are still unclear.<br /> <br /> Mainly because the Requiem 2nd Ed book offers little rituals, any Circle of the Crone player with Cr\u00faac will have to resort to the old books for some more, but our discussion became about what is thematically 'canon' with the new Circle of the Crone or not.<br /> <br /> For example, in the first edition of the game the Acolytes were closely tied with the Spirit World, and many of their sorceries reflected that. Are those still thematically appropriated? My friend pointed out that in Blood Sorcery the Onyx Path was already drifting AWAY from spirits, but I remain unconvinced. Did Rose or Machinev say anything about it? Or anyone for that matter? What do you think?<br /> <br /> Another thing I want to ask is that Rose stated they are releasing many 1st Ed rituals in the dev blog, and she has a list already (refer to the Acolyte Merits comment section). Does anyone know if those are anywhere near of being posted, if there is any progression on that front or if that is even happening at all? I was hoping that would offer me further clues aswell!<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:49:30-08:00","id":424088,"title":"","content":"No drifting away from spirits, no. What Blood Sorcery (including Cruac) is not capable of doing is to mess up with otherworlds, that includes the shadow. Fortunately (for the sorcerer, unfortunately for anyone else) spirits don't remain in their side of the gauntlet, so there are spirits roaming around in the physical realm, Cruac is perfectly capable of summoning, controling and bindding those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":".  grammar 03-01-2015, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:43:53-08:00","id":424151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/424040-requiem-2nd-ed-vs-cr\u00faac-sorcery-what-is-canon#post424040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing I want to ask is that Rose stated they are releasing many 1st Ed rituals in the dev blog, and she has a list already (refer to the Acolyte Merits comment section). Does anyone know if those are anywhere near of being posted, if there is any progression on that front or if that is even happening at all? I was hoping that would offer me further clues aswell!<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading!</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about updated 1E rituals, but there's a bunch of 2E rituals in the preview for the Circle of the Crone section in Secrets of the Covenants. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1eJz_HsiLvwF8e4okeCDF-FzV-japjrLxmd9bx4diVSc/mobilebasic?pli=1#h.fa1iuqyou3x6\" target=\"_blank\">here[</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T11:08:40-08:00","id":424313,"title":"","content":"I would say they are drifting away from spirits, as in the Hisil. Vampires have their own spiritual antagonists, the strix, and Cruac is much more closely tied to that than before. There's even a Cruac Style in that link Charlaquin posted that calls up a shadowy strix-like thing. Its kinda like an ephemeral being familiar thing. Its not a spirit from the Hisil, though.<br /> <br /> In 1e, there was a very werewolf-y animism / shamanism vibe that Cruac adopted. I think that its safe to say that the Crone has moved away from that.<br /> <br /> EDIT - I think there's a blurb in the Blood Sorcery book about not dealing with the Hisil to an extent too. I don't remember exactly.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think the big difference is going to focus around the tonal change that the Circle has adopted. The CotC book of 1e feels pretty different than 2e, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-01-2015, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:33:26-08:00","id":424644,"title":"","content":"Thematically, the only ritual that has ever been stricken down was the Theban rain of fire one. The spirit spells are still canon, thematically. Mechanically, they might need some work. Until the update is done, the main things that need to be considered are the GMC rules on spirits and Kindred sorcery can't summon spirits, only Strix. The sorcery works on spirits that are already present, nearby, in the &quot;real&quot; world. The spirit world, Shadow, is what is out of bounds. Spirits in Shadow, ghosts in the Underworld, are beyond the reach of Kindred sorcery. Pretty much what everyone else said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T21:10:51-08:00","id":424858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/424040-requiem-2nd-ed-vs-cr\u00faac-sorcery-what-is-canon?p=424644#post424644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thematically, the only ritual that has ever been stricken down was the Theban rain of fire one. The spirit spells are still canon, thematically. Mechanically, they might need some work. Until the update is done, the main things that need to be considered are the GMC rules on spirits and Kindred sorcery can't summon spirits, only Strix. The sorcery works on spirits that are already present, nearby, in the &quot;real&quot; world. The spirit world, Shadow, is what is out of bounds. Spirits in Shadow, ghosts in the Underworld, are beyond the reach of Kindred sorcery. Pretty much what everyone else said.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were optional in the Crone book and explicitly noted as &quot;This sort of breaks with what we've said elsewhere, but if you want it, here...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T23:03:26-08:00","id":424910,"title":"","content":"The book <i>explicitly</i> says the rituals are optional. Optional does not mean non-canon. We are talking about a sandbox style game so the entire book is <i>implicitly</i> optional. The book notes &quot;Spirits are an inherent part of the World of Darkness, of which Vampire and the other games are each just one part.&quot; (p.14) &quot;This sort of breaks with what we've said elsewhere...&quot; is not found in the book. The optional part comes from Mage has spirit rules and Werewolf has spirit rules and now Vampire is getting in the mix, but doesn't have spirit rules so there is a jumbled mess (debate on which is right and there is no canon answer). GMC came up with a new set of rules, which as far as I know, will be the basis for every line's spirit rules in 2E so when the rituals are updated (they were submitted for the update because of the mess) they would be no more or less optional than the rituals in Blood Sorcery for instance. OP published them and never printed in a later book that kindred sorcery doesn't affect spirits. I wouldn't use the rituals as they are, but the basic function and name are exactly what the writers want Cruac users to have in their repertoire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T03:43:28-08:00","id":424991,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt; Kindred sorcery can't summon spirits, only Strix. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> That's not the impression I got from the new Cruac casting style and spells. Opening portals to who knows where and pulling things out to act as servants, conjuring familiars, trapping the ghost of a murdered victim into inanimate objects, forcing the deceased's spirit back into it's corpse temporarily (which incidentally used to be a Theban ritual.) doesn't say to me that such things are beyond the purview of Kindred sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:28:20-08:00","id":425541,"title":"","content":"In this case, &quot;summon spirits&quot; means to call forth Spirits from Shadow or Ghosts from the Underworld. Cruac can deal with Spirits and Ghosts that are already present, manifested or not. Any portals Cruac opens are to someplace other than Shadow, Underworld, Hedge, or any other line's little other realm of existence. Don't know where Cruac pulls spirits from, only where it does not pull them from. The limits of kindred sorcery are very specific and not particularly limiting. It becomes necessary to split hairs when so many different things have the same name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}